# Architecture

EstateX is a premium real-estate marketplace: Next.js (`apps/web`) + NestJS (`apps/api`) + PostgreSQL/Prisma.

- Follow `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/database.md`, and `docs/api.md`.
- Work phase by phase. Do not implement unrelated features in the same change.
- Prefer reusable modules over copy-paste. Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
- Keep business logic out of Nest controllers and out of React page files.
- Keep API envelopes consistent: `{ success, data, meta?, message?, code? }`.
- Shared enums and DTOs belong in `packages/types` when both apps need them.
- Never hardcode secrets. Use env vars from `.env.example`.
- Inspect existing code before adding files. Match naming and folder patterns already in the repo.
